those press releases

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:44.771
and if you look at the,

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:48.041
of all places the New York
Times did a story a week ago

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:49.342
about

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:53.012
the circulation of
what I'm saying is

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:54.781
essentially as big.

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:57.417
It's very big and the
word is getting out.

00:01:57.417 --> 00:01:59.486
I did a couple of them today.

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:02.689
I like because I'm
not confined as to

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:05.091
number of characters but you
know the number of characters,

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:06.559 align:start size:84% position:16%
you don't want to keep
it too long anyway,

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:09.262 align:start size:97% position:3%
okay that's one thing we
all learned maybe from that.

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:11.998
No, I, I think, I think
we're doing very well.

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:13.500
With that being said,

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:15.435
I'll be on social media in
the not too distant future.

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:16.736
We're looking at
a lot of options.

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:18.104
We had,

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:19.606 align:start size:84% position:16%
a hundreds of
millions of people,

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:21.274
you know, if you look at,

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:23.076
we had 91 on one site,

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:24.177
we had 10 on another,

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:25.578
we had 36 on another,

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:27.147
we had Potus,

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:31.684
we have a lot of people and
a lot of people on Facebook

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:34.254
and I hear it's become
very boring to be honest

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:37.223 align:start size:88% position:13%
and I hear in particular
Twitter's become
very, very boring

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:39.425
and a lot of conservative
voices have gotten off.

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:42.562
Some have been thrown out and
a lot of them have gotten off

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:44.397
and I hear Twitter
is not doing well

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:46.032
and it's lost it's voice

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:49.435
and when I started there
like 11 or 12 years ago,

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:51.004
it was not a success.

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:53.239
I mean it was not a, I don't
know it was going to make it

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:54.774
but it was not a success.

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:58.378
It became very successful and
I think you're going to see

00:02:58.378 --> 00:03:00.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of people are going
to be finding other,

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:03.049
other, there's a lot
of platforms out there.

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:04.417
That's what we're looking at.

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:07.086 align:start size:97% position:3%
Getting the right platform,
a perfect platform

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:10.223
and I think you'll see
something fairly soon.

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:11.457
- Yeah, that's great to hear

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:13.626
and as, as you may know
I've been talking to,

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:15.862 align:start size:84% position:16%
to some of your guys
about locals.com

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:18.198
which is the tech company
I started so we shall see.

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:19.666
- Good.

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:20.967
- So, you know, I've told
my audience many times

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:23.403
that one of the reasons that I,

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:27.073 align:start size:97% position:3%
I didn't support you in
2016 but then I did in 2020

00:03:27.073 --> 00:03:28.575 line:0%
was that I started going back

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:31.511 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
and watching old
videos of you on Oprah

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:33.012 line:0%
and on David Letterman

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.681 line:0%
and on Phil Donahue

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:37.183 line:0%
and I realized that you
were basically saying

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:41.721 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
the exact same things 30 years
ago that you're saying now

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:45.592
and what that made me
wonder was sort of,

00:03:45.592 --> 00:03:47.560
did you always, you know,
they would always ask you,

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.195
Oprah would say, "Oh, you
should run for President",

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:50.697
or Donahue would say it but

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:53.967 align:start position:0%
did you always feel that
somebody else was going to do it

00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:56.169
and then you just got
pinned into doing it

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:58.871 align:start size:97% position:3%
because you didn't seem to
really want to do it actually,

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:00.873 align:start size:84% position:16%
you kind of wanted
somebody else to do it

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:02.375 align:start size:88% position:13%
from the way I read it?
- It's a great,

00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:04.510
I've, nobody's ever asked
me the question that way

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:05.945
and it's very interesting.

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:08.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah I assumed that
somebody else would do it

00:04:08.481 --> 00:04:10.917
because people cannot be
that stupid (Dave scoffs)

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:14.153 align:start size:84% position:16%
to be taken
advantage of by China

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:15.722
and in particular at that time

00:04:15.722 --> 00:04:17.223
if you go back 20 or 30 years,

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:19.192
it was Japan was really
doing a number on us

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:22.862 align:start size:84% position:16%
and it's all the
same and frankly it
hasn't changed because

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:25.898
whether it's China, Japan,
or many others, I mean it's,

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:29.502 align:start size:97% position:3%
they're all taking but
China obviously right now is

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:31.004
the head of the pack

00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:32.839
and I always felt
that somebody else,

00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:34.307
nobody's ever asked it this way,

00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:36.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've always felt that
somebody else would do it

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:39.279
and they didn't

00:04:39.279 --> 00:04:41.414
and it went for a long time,
you know, those interviews

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:42.882
and one thing you
have to say David,

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:44.751
if nothing else
I was consistent.

00:04:44.751 --> 00:04:46.052 align:start size:81% position:19%
- I mean it was...
- Yeah.

00:04:46.052 --> 00:04:47.553
- I've seen it too where I,

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:50.990
I've seen recently a replay
of some of the statements and

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:53.760 align:start size:88% position:13%
they're almost identical
to what I say now

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:54.861
and I was right.

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:55.795
I was right.

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:58.731
We have now 30 trillion in debt.

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:00.667
We have a country that is just,

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:03.303
it's just ridiculous what's
going on in so many ways.

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:05.004 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'd talked about
the border even then

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:06.706
and people coming in

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:10.076 align:start size:97% position:3%
and you know, the wrong
people coming in in many cases

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:11.744 align:start size:97% position:3%
and you see what's
happening where the prisons

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:13.579
are being emptied out
in other countries

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:15.948
and they're coming
into our country

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:17.483
and I was,

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:19.152
yeah very consistent.

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:20.486
It's very interesting.

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:21.988
- Yeah.

00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:23.256
When did you realize that
you were going to fully

00:05:23.256 --> 00:05:25.024
have to say what you thought?

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:27.393 align:start size:97% position:3%
Because when I started going
to some of your rallies

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:29.495 align:start size:81% position:19%
and I'm here in
crazy Los Angeles,

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:31.698
I was going to the Trump
rallies in Beverly Hills

00:05:31.698 --> 00:05:33.666
and it was a joy fest.

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:35.968
Like it was, it was
truly unbelievable,

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:37.537
I couldn't believe
it and the main thing

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:39.939
people would say to me when
they would come, they'd say,

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:42.775 align:start size:97% position:3%
"Dave, you know, I'm just
sick of being called a racist

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:44.911 align:start size:97% position:3%
and a homophobe and a
bigot and everything else."

00:05:44.911 --> 00:05:46.112
And I met these people,

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:48.081 align:start size:84% position:16%
these were the nicest,
joyous, happiest,

00:05:48.081 --> 00:05:49.315 align:start size:84% position:16%
decent Americans ever.
- Great people.

00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:50.483
- But when did you realize

00:05:50.483 --> 00:05:52.018 align:start size:88% position:13%
that you were just
going to have to sort of

00:05:52.018 --> 00:05:55.088
walk through that fire and
take those, those labels?

00:05:56.222 --> 00:05:57.657 align:start size:88% position:13%
- So a lot of people
think I was going to run

00:05:57.657 --> 00:05:59.192
like for a long time.

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:01.294
You know they were asking me
that question 30 years ago,

00:06:01.294 --> 00:06:04.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
as you would say and
Oprah was and Donahue was,

00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:06.132
and they were all doing it and,

00:06:06.132 --> 00:06:09.035
and I'd give the answer
that I doubt it because

00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:11.471
believe it or not Dave,
I'm a very honest person

00:06:11.471 --> 00:06:13.906
and you know, I'm not
sure that you can be

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:15.708
honest and be in politics, okay?

00:06:15.708 --> 00:06:18.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I never really thought
I was going to do it.

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:20.279
A lot of people thought I was
going to do it 8 years ago,

00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:21.581
12 years ago.

00:06:21.581 --> 00:06:24.984
I think probably it
really hit me when

00:06:24.984 --> 00:06:27.787 align:start size:97% position:3%
I turned down a big
extension on The Apprentice.

00:06:27.787 --> 00:06:29.589 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know, the show was
a very big success,

00:06:29.589 --> 00:06:33.426 align:start size:88% position:13%
I did it for 14 seasons,
can you believe it?

00:06:33.426 --> 00:06:34.660 align:start size:88% position:13%
And then Schwarzenegger
and Mo...

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:36.129 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I watched, I watched
I miss Joan Rivers,

00:06:36.129 --> 00:06:37.463
I miss Joan Rivers man.

00:06:37.463 --> 00:06:39.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
She was, she was the best.
- Oh yeah.

00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:40.666
Oh yeah, she wanted to come on

00:06:40.666 --> 00:06:41.934
and they all wanted to come on.

00:06:41.934 --> 00:06:44.137 align:start size:84% position:16%
I watch Erin
Burnett, you know now

00:06:44.137 --> 00:06:46.305
but she would beg me
to get on the show.

00:06:46.305 --> 00:06:47.940 align:start size:84% position:16%
She, she was on
three or four times,

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:51.010
she would virtually beg me
to be on, The Apprentice

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:55.314 align:start size:97% position:3%
and now I watch her hit
from all sides on MSD and C,

00:06:55.314 --> 00:06:57.683
I don't watch her very much
but I see she's on there

00:06:57.683 --> 00:06:58.918
and I assume she's as

00:06:58.918 --> 00:07:01.387
nothing but bad but she
would beg to be on as,

00:07:01.387 --> 00:07:02.955
as did others,

00:07:02.955 --> 00:07:04.056
as did many others.

00:07:04.056 --> 00:07:05.958
But the show was
a great success,

00:07:05.958 --> 00:07:08.494
and they wanted to extend it

00:07:08.494 --> 00:07:09.328
a lot,

00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:10.663
like at

00:07:10.663 --> 00:07:11.898
the highest level,

00:07:11.898 --> 00:07:14.000
they came over to my
office and I said,

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:15.635
"No, I got to, I
have to do this,

00:07:15.635 --> 00:07:17.036
I have to run for President."

00:07:17.036 --> 00:07:18.771
And they thought I was kidding.

00:07:18.771 --> 00:07:20.673
They didn't want to hear it.

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:21.941
They wanted to extend the show.

00:07:21.941 --> 00:07:23.576
They ended up getting
Arnold Schwarzenegger

00:07:23.576 --> 00:07:24.844
who failed badly as you
know, (Dave chuckles)

00:07:24.844 --> 00:07:27.346
he was off in like,
a matter of minutes

00:07:27.346 --> 00:07:29.749 align:start size:97% position:3%
and they also, during the
time they get Martha Stewart

00:07:29.749 --> 00:07:31.284
and she failed

00:07:31.284 --> 00:07:33.553
but we had a great success
and it was for many years

00:07:33.553 --> 00:07:34.687
and I said, "No."

00:07:34.687 --> 00:07:36.155
And you know,

00:07:36.155 --> 00:07:38.391 align:start size:97% position:3%
when you turn down a primetime
show long-term extension,

00:07:38.391 --> 00:07:40.293
it's a lot of money no
matter how rich you are,

00:07:40.293 --> 00:07:42.028
but it's a lot of money

00:07:42.028 --> 00:07:44.030
and a lot of prestige

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:45.264
and I turned them down.

00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:47.600
The top executives
of NBC came over

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:49.335
and they wanted to make a deal

00:07:49.335 --> 00:07:52.972
and I turned them down and
I guess so that was really

00:07:52.972 --> 00:07:54.640
when I thought I
was going to do it

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:58.444 align:start size:97% position:3%
and then of course the famous
ride down the escalator

00:07:58.444 --> 00:07:59.579
and that was it, Dave.

00:07:59.579 --> 00:08:00.780
That was it.

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:03.115 align:start size:88% position:13%
Once I rode down the
escalator with our great

00:08:03.115 --> 00:08:05.818
First Lady that, that
turned out to be it.

00:08:06.886 --> 00:08:09.622 align:start size:84% position:16%
- When did you
realize how connected

00:08:09.622 --> 00:08:12.391
the sort of mainstream
media was to the swamp?

00:08:12.391 --> 00:08:14.227
You know, you were talking
about draining the swamp

00:08:14.227 --> 00:08:16.362
and obviously the media
was going after you,

00:08:16.362 --> 00:08:17.997
and you started punching back

00:08:17.997 --> 00:08:20.266 align:start position:0%
and Republicans or Conservatives
or people on the right

00:08:20.266 --> 00:08:22.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
usually don't punch back.
- They don't.

00:08:22.535 --> 00:08:24.103
- Yeah, did you realize it,

00:08:24.103 --> 00:08:25.338
was it by the time
you were President

00:08:25.338 --> 00:08:27.240 align:start size:88% position:13%
that you fully realized
or it was really,

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:29.075
was it that first debate?

00:08:29.075 --> 00:08:30.810 align:start size:81% position:19%
- No, I thought
it was bad frankly

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:32.378
but I never knew it was this bad

00:08:32.378 --> 00:08:34.046
and now it's worse
than ever before.

00:08:34.046 --> 00:08:35.982
Now it's so ridiculous I mean,

00:08:35.982 --> 00:08:37.483
you see

00:08:37.483 --> 00:08:40.953
where Biden gets up and says
things that nobody can believe

00:08:40.953 --> 00:08:44.690 align:start size:97% position:3%
or doesn't say things and
they say, "Could that be FDR?"

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:46.259
FDR, great speaker

00:08:46.259 --> 00:08:49.095 align:start size:97% position:3%
and you know now, now it's,
it's out of control but

00:08:50.263 --> 00:08:52.732 align:start size:84% position:16%
I've always known
that they were shaky

00:08:52.732 --> 00:08:55.501 align:start size:97% position:3%
but I used to get great press,
you know, before I ran for,

00:08:55.501 --> 00:08:57.803
I guess that's probably
one of the reasons I won,

00:08:57.803 --> 00:08:59.739
before I ran for President,

00:08:59.739 --> 00:09:01.040
I got a lot of great press.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:03.409
I was getting, I was the king.

00:09:03.409 --> 00:09:05.811 align:start size:84% position:16%
I was getting
pressed like nobody

00:09:05.811 --> 00:09:07.213
and you know, I did fine

00:09:07.213 --> 00:09:08.848
but I also understood

00:09:10.182 --> 00:09:13.753 align:start position:0%
where and how they were
functioning as much as you can.

00:09:13.753 --> 00:09:16.055
Nobody understands the press
fully to be honest with you,

00:09:16.055 --> 00:09:18.391
I don't care how well
you do with it but

00:09:18.391 --> 00:09:19.859
once I announced

00:09:19.859 --> 00:09:22.361
and when I made the first
speech in Trump Tower,

00:09:22.361 --> 00:09:24.897
once I got down from the
escalator I will tell you,

00:09:26.299 --> 00:09:29.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would say the press
turned radically different

00:09:29.302 --> 00:09:30.937 align:start size:84% position:16%
and now they've
become very corrupt.

00:09:30.937 --> 00:09:32.138
I mean, they're really corrupt.

00:09:32.138 --> 00:09:34.340 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's a, it's a terrible
thing to watch.

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:35.975
We don't have freedom
of the press anymore,

00:09:35.975 --> 00:09:38.311
we don't have free
press or fair press.

00:09:38.311 --> 00:09:40.980
We have a very, very
corrupt press and,

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:42.949
and you don't even have
to get into the argument

00:09:42.949 --> 00:09:44.183
although you say plenty, you,

00:09:44.183 --> 00:09:45.451
you have strong opinions on it

00:09:45.451 --> 00:09:48.354
but we have a very,
very corrupted media.

00:09:48.354 --> 00:09:50.089
- Yeah, no, they're,
they're long gone.

00:09:50.089 --> 00:09:51.624
They're activists
not journalists.

00:09:51.624 --> 00:09:52.491
- They're gonzo.

00:09:52.491 --> 00:09:53.726
They're gonzo.

00:09:53.726 --> 00:09:56.529
We're doing a big one in
Ohio on Saturday night

00:09:56.529 --> 00:09:58.764
and people are already
lined up and you know,

00:09:58.764 --> 00:10:01.367
there's just been a great
connection to the people.

00:10:01.367 --> 00:10:03.536 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
I've had a great
connection to the people

00:10:03.536 --> 00:10:05.404 line:0%
and it's amazing because

00:10:05.404 --> 00:10:08.374 line:0%
when you get virtually a
hundred percent bad press

00:10:08.374 --> 00:10:10.276
and Fox is a whole
different ball game

00:10:10.276 --> 00:10:12.078
from what it was too by the way,

00:10:12.078 --> 00:10:15.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
but when you get a hundred
percent anti-press,

00:10:15.615 --> 00:10:18.618 align:start size:88% position:13%
it's just, look you
have some really great,

00:10:18.618 --> 00:10:20.553
great people who should
have gotten the Pulitzer,

00:10:20.553 --> 00:10:22.588 align:start size:97% position:3%
you have people that called
Russia, Russia, Russia

00:10:22.588 --> 00:10:23.723
exactly right.

00:10:23.723 --> 00:10:24.924
They don't get the Pulitzer,

00:10:24.924 --> 00:10:26.092
they give Pulitzer Prizes

00:10:26.092 --> 00:10:27.893 align:start size:84% position:16%
to people that
were totally wrong.

00:10:27.893 --> 00:10:28.894
Totally wrong.

00:10:28.894 --> 00:10:30.262
It's a disgrace.

00:10:30.262 --> 00:10:32.965
But when you have that,
and it's amazing that

00:10:32.965 --> 00:10:34.367
even in the last election,

00:10:34.367 --> 00:10:36.902
I got far more votes
in the last election

00:10:36.902 --> 00:10:41.207
and did far better than I did
in the first election in 2016

00:10:41.207 --> 00:10:45.211
and it's amazing that you can
have the press so against you,

00:10:45.211 --> 00:10:46.445
big tech against you,

00:10:46.445 --> 00:10:48.714 align:start size:84% position:16%
and you end up getting
75 million votes,

00:10:48.714 --> 00:10:50.783
which is the highest
anybody's ever gotten

00:10:50.783 --> 00:10:52.218
as a sitting President.

00:10:52.218 --> 00:10:54.120
It's, it's pretty busy,

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:56.455
but what it shows you is that

00:10:56.455 --> 00:10:59.058
the people of our
country get it.

00:10:59.058 --> 00:10:59.892
They really get it.

00:10:59.892 --> 00:11:01.227
It's pretty amazing.

00:11:01.227 --> 00:11:02.628
- Yeah are, are,

00:11:02.628 --> 00:11:04.296 align:start size:97% position:3%
you must be incredibly
psyched to get back out there

00:11:04.296 --> 00:11:05.765
with the people

00:11:05.765 --> 00:11:06.999 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I know you're doing some
shows with Bill O'Reilly

00:11:06.999 --> 00:11:07.933
and the rallies are
gonna start up again.

00:11:07.933 --> 00:11:09.168
I mean to me it's just that,

00:11:09.168 --> 00:11:11.237
people just want to be
proud of America again.

00:11:11.237 --> 00:11:13.205 align:start size:84% position:16%
I can't wait til they
start up rallies,

00:11:13.205 --> 00:11:14.440
whether you're there or not

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:16.575
just to get people out
there and holding flags

00:11:16.575 --> 00:11:18.477
and being proud to
be Americans again.

00:11:18.477 --> 00:11:20.079
- Well, we're doing
a big one in Florida,

00:11:20.079 --> 00:11:21.614
I guess it's July 3rd

00:11:21.614 --> 00:11:23.983
and we're doing a big one
in Ohio on Saturday night

00:11:23.983 --> 00:11:25.651 align:start size:84% position:16%
and we're, we're going
to start doing it

00:11:25.651 --> 00:11:27.787
just to give people
some pride again.

00:11:27.787 --> 00:11:29.689
It's not, you know, it's early

00:11:29.689 --> 00:11:31.057
but it's not really
early because...

00:11:31.057 --> 00:11:32.992 line:0%
(beep)

00:11:36.529 --> 00:11:37.797
You know, they want to know,

00:11:37.797 --> 00:11:39.498
they want to have a
voice out there and

00:11:39.498 --> 00:11:41.067
you don't get it from the media.

00:11:41.067 --> 00:11:42.568
They don't give you a fair voice

00:11:42.568 --> 00:11:45.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
so you have to do it a
little bit differently and

00:11:45.237 --> 00:11:46.572
you know, in the one case,

00:11:46.572 --> 00:11:48.407
sending out those press releases

00:11:48.407 --> 00:11:50.910
they get onto Twitter and
they get onto Facebook

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:53.779 align:start size:88% position:13%
and they get on to
everything I mean it's,

00:11:53.779 --> 00:11:55.247
it's been, that's been amazing

00:11:55.247 --> 00:11:57.016
but the voice that
really gets out,

00:11:57.016 --> 00:12:00.586 align:start position:0%
is the voice at the rallies
because they cover the rallies,

00:12:00.586 --> 00:12:02.621
you know, they cover the
rallies because of ratings.

00:12:02.621 --> 00:12:05.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
The one thing ratings
are most important, okay?

00:12:05.558 --> 00:12:07.093
If you get great ratings,

00:12:07.093 --> 00:12:09.295
they're going to cover you
no matter what you say and

00:12:09.295 --> 00:12:11.464
we get a lot of coverage and,

00:12:11.464 --> 00:12:12.932
and I think it's very important

00:12:12.932 --> 00:12:14.500
and that's what the people want

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:16.769
because they love the country,

00:12:16.769 --> 00:12:18.204
they hate open borders,

00:12:18.204 --> 00:12:22.575 align:start size:88% position:13%
they hate, you know,
sanctuary cities protect

00:12:22.575 --> 00:12:24.510 align:start size:88% position:13%
people that are
criminals in many cases.

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:27.379
I mean the sanctuary cities,
they hate, defund the police.

00:12:27.379 --> 00:12:29.048
Think of the policies
these people have;

00:12:29.048 --> 00:12:29.882
defund the police,

00:12:29.882 --> 00:12:30.816
sanctuary cities,

00:12:30.816 --> 00:12:32.318
open borders,

00:12:32.318 --> 00:12:34.620
let anybody come into our
country criminal or not

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:36.122
and it's supposed
to be all wonderful

00:12:36.122 --> 00:12:37.857
and now cancel culture

00:12:37.857 --> 00:12:39.725 align:start size:97% position:3%
and all of the other
things you're seeing on the

00:12:39.725 --> 00:12:41.260
school boards, right?

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:42.695
And they're supposed to win?

00:12:42.695 --> 00:12:45.498 align:start size:97% position:3%
I don't, I don't believe
they can win with that and...

00:12:45.498 --> 00:12:47.433 line:0%
(beep)

00:12:52.705 --> 00:12:55.808
Because those are
not 50% issues.

00:12:55.808 --> 00:12:57.042
Let's,

00:12:57.042 --> 00:12:59.779
as an example we talked
about energy, right?

00:12:59.779 --> 00:13:02.681
During the debates,
during the campaign,

00:13:02.681 --> 00:13:05.484 align:start size:97% position:3%
and we're energy independent
but we're not any longer.

00:13:05.484 --> 00:13:08.320 align:start position:0%
Now we're going to have to start
buying from the Middle East

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:10.422
and Russia and all
these other places.

00:13:10.422 --> 00:13:11.924
We were energy independent.

00:13:11.924 --> 00:13:14.193
Now we're not because they
canceled a lot of deals,

00:13:14.193 --> 00:13:15.361
canceled the pipeline,

00:13:15.361 --> 00:13:17.062 align:start size:84% position:16%
how about canceling
the pipeline,

00:13:17.062 --> 00:13:21.066 align:start size:97% position:3%
but letting Russia have its
pipeline to Europe and Germany

00:13:21.066 --> 00:13:22.501
and it's just,

00:13:22.501 --> 00:13:26.038 align:start position:0%
it's I don't believe that those
policies are anywhere near

00:13:26.038 --> 00:13:27.773
50% but I think...

00:13:27.773 --> 00:13:29.675 line:0%
(beep)

00:13:35.714 --> 00:13:38.184
- Yeah, I think my 10%
that you predicted about

00:13:38.184 --> 00:13:39.785 align:start position:0%
staying on YouTube may have
just dropped to 5%, but that...

00:13:39.785 --> 00:13:41.086
- I think you're finished.

00:13:41.086 --> 00:13:43.756
Let me reduce it.
Yeah. (chuckles)

00:13:43.756 --> 00:13:44.590
- That's all right.

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:45.825
That's all right.

00:13:45.825 --> 00:13:47.026
Let me just ask you a
couple of other things,

00:13:47.026 --> 00:13:47.827 align:start size:88% position:13%
'cause I want to be
respectful of your time.

00:13:47.827 --> 00:13:49.261
Were you ever really,

00:13:49.261 --> 00:13:51.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
were you ever really
worried about impeachment?

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:53.933
Because I saw you, I don't
know if you remember this,

00:13:53.933 --> 00:13:56.669
but we actually met
briefly at Mar-a-Lago

00:13:56.669 --> 00:13:59.939
back in December of,
I guess it was 2018

00:13:59.939 --> 00:14:01.874
and I had seen you
speak that afternoon

00:14:01.874 --> 00:14:03.375
at a turning point event

00:14:03.375 --> 00:14:05.344
and it was in the midst
of the impeachment thing.

00:14:05.344 --> 00:14:07.112
Dan Crenshaw went
on stage with you

00:14:07.112 --> 00:14:08.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
and brought out his piece
of paper that showed,

00:14:08.814 --> 00:14:10.983
you know, he didn't
vote for it and, but,

00:14:10.983 --> 00:14:12.218
but everybody was saying,

00:14:12.218 --> 00:14:13.853
"The walls are closing
in, he's freaking out."

00:14:13.853 --> 00:14:16.121 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I saw you that
night you had no tie on,

00:14:16.121 --> 00:14:17.022
you were relaxed,

00:14:17.022 --> 00:14:18.257
you were laughing.

00:14:18.257 --> 00:14:20.593 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like, were you ever
really, really worried

00:14:20.593 --> 00:14:22.595 align:start size:84% position:16%
or even on the
second time around?

00:14:22.595 --> 00:14:24.430
- Well they had no
proof either time.

00:14:24.430 --> 00:14:25.564
They had no proof

00:14:25.564 --> 00:14:27.132
and frankly,

00:14:27.132 --> 00:14:29.468 align:start size:97% position:3%
you know, I have a lot of good
relationships in Congress,

00:14:29.468 --> 00:14:31.670
in the Senate and in the House

00:14:31.670 --> 00:14:34.506 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I will say this
Richard Nixon did not.

00:14:34.506 --> 00:14:35.674
Now he also had,

00:14:35.674 --> 00:14:37.443
you know, 300 tapes, right?

00:14:37.443 --> 00:14:38.711
That didn't help him.

00:14:38.711 --> 00:14:41.547
The tapes weren't
exactly positive,

00:14:41.547 --> 00:14:43.148
they were a total disaster

00:14:43.148 --> 00:14:45.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I have a lot of great
friends in Congress.

00:14:45.885 --> 00:14:48.220
Jim Jordan and so many others.

00:14:48.220 --> 00:14:49.221
Banks and

00:14:50.589 --> 00:14:51.790
Debbie Lesko,

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:54.426 align:start size:81% position:19%
I just have so
many great friends

00:14:54.426 --> 00:14:57.396 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I felt in the
same way in the Senate

00:14:57.396 --> 00:14:59.031
I have a lot of great
friends in the Senate

00:14:59.031 --> 00:15:01.533
and I didn't feel that
assuming I was innocent,

00:15:01.533 --> 00:15:04.803 align:start size:97% position:3%
I didn't feel that they
would sail me down the river

00:15:04.803 --> 00:15:07.273
and I, you know, I
felt very confident

00:15:07.273 --> 00:15:09.208
and you know, you'd see
CNN where they'd say,

00:15:09.208 --> 00:15:10.943
"He's walking in
the White House,

00:15:10.943 --> 00:15:12.478
he's walking in his room."

00:15:12.478 --> 00:15:14.079
And I'd be in the
Oval Office, right?

00:15:14.079 --> 00:15:15.981
I'd be, you know, not even...

00:15:15.981 --> 00:15:18.050
I'll never forget, I was
with a group of people.

00:15:18.050 --> 00:15:20.686 align:start size:97% position:3%
Very, very big business
people from another country

00:15:20.686 --> 00:15:23.822
having to do with bringing
business to this country,

00:15:23.822 --> 00:15:26.191 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I'll never
forget it Dave where

00:15:26.191 --> 00:15:28.627
the television was
on and CNN was saying

00:15:28.627 --> 00:15:31.363 align:start position:0%
I was up in my bedroom, storming
the bed, (Dave chuckles)

00:15:31.363 --> 00:15:33.465
and I'm in the Oval Office
with these business people

00:15:33.465 --> 00:15:36.302
trying to get them
to invest in America

00:15:36.302 --> 00:15:38.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they said, "Wow,
that's really dishonest."

00:15:38.237 --> 00:15:40.439
I said, "That's what
I've been saying."

00:15:40.439 --> 00:15:42.441 align:start size:84% position:16%
No, there's tremendous
dishonesty Dave.

00:15:42.441 --> 00:15:44.009
Tremendous.

00:15:44.009 --> 00:15:46.045 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Alright. Last question
for you, for now

00:15:46.045 --> 00:15:48.714
and then I hope we get to do
this in person at some point.

00:15:48.714 --> 00:15:50.215 align:start size:75% position:25%
- Sure. We will.
- This is,

00:15:50.215 --> 00:15:52.418
I never, I've literally never
done this in any interview,

00:15:52.418 --> 00:15:54.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've never asked the
audience to ask a question

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:56.789
but I thought let's try
this with President Trump

00:15:56.789 --> 00:15:59.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there were many
versions of this question

00:15:59.758 --> 00:16:01.360
which basically is,

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:04.296 align:start size:88% position:13%
that pretty much
everybody doesn't think
Biden is in charge.

00:16:04.296 --> 00:16:06.365
Nobody really thinks
he's running the show.

00:16:06.365 --> 00:16:07.566
So the question

00:16:07.566 --> 00:16:09.001
is something to the effect of,

00:16:09.001 --> 00:16:11.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
who do you think is
really running this thing?

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:13.038
Is this the Obama machine?

00:16:13.038 --> 00:16:14.239
Is this the Clinton machine?

00:16:14.239 --> 00:16:15.574 line:0%
Is this something else?

00:16:15.574 --> 00:16:18.377 line:0%
What do you really think
is happening right now?

00:16:18.377 --> 00:16:20.546 line:0%
- I think it's a
group of people and

00:16:20.546 --> 00:16:23.382
a lot of people say
Susan Rice and Obama

00:16:23.382 --> 00:16:24.917
and a lot of people say

00:16:24.917 --> 00:16:26.952
perhaps Clinton to
a lesser extent,

00:16:26.952 --> 00:16:29.188
although she never got
along with Biden and

00:16:29.188 --> 00:16:31.056 align:start size:84% position:16%
she's very, very angry
because she said,

00:16:31.056 --> 00:16:32.424
why didn't you do that for her?

00:16:32.424 --> 00:16:33.392
You know, she was saying...

00:16:33.392 --> 00:16:35.327 line:0%
(beep)

00:16:36.562 --> 00:16:38.397
because it's, it was far easier

00:16:38.397 --> 00:16:40.299
'cause that race was far closer

00:16:40.299 --> 00:16:44.003
than the race we just
had, the 2020 race and

00:16:44.003 --> 00:16:47.272
but you have people
that it's, it's a,

00:16:47.272 --> 00:16:48.841
it's a group of people.

00:16:48.841 --> 00:16:51.010
I don't think it's Biden frankly

00:16:51.010 --> 00:16:52.244
and I,

00:16:52.244 --> 00:16:53.912
you know, in many
ways I wish it were

00:16:53.912 --> 00:16:56.015
because that's the way
it's supposed to be,

00:16:56.015 --> 00:16:57.282
but I don't believe it is

00:16:57.282 --> 00:17:00.419
and maybe Harris to an extent,

00:17:00.419 --> 00:17:02.554 align:start size:97% position:3%
although I don't think
she's distinguishing herself

00:17:02.554 --> 00:17:04.556
with her, her border
trips (Dave scoffs)

00:17:04.556 --> 00:17:06.258
and now all of a sudden, I said,

00:17:06.258 --> 00:17:08.460
as soon as I announced that
I'm going to the border,

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:10.963
I actually made a minor bet.

00:17:10.963 --> 00:17:12.431
I said, watch what happens,

00:17:12.431 --> 00:17:14.233
she's going to announce and
right after I announced,

00:17:14.233 --> 00:17:16.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
as you know, she announced
that she's going down,

00:17:16.068 --> 00:17:18.504
I guess she's going
tomorrow or something

00:17:18.504 --> 00:17:20.739 align:start size:88% position:13%
but she would have
never gone to the border

00:17:20.739 --> 00:17:22.074
and I'm going next week.

00:17:22.074 --> 00:17:23.342
So,

00:17:23.342 --> 00:17:25.110
I think it's just
a group of people.

00:17:25.110 --> 00:17:27.279 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean, think of it
when he signed those 17

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:29.748
declarations,

00:17:29.748 --> 00:17:30.849
special orders,

00:17:30.849 --> 00:17:32.718
presidential orders,

00:17:32.718 --> 00:17:34.386
he signed them

00:17:34.386 --> 00:17:36.055 align:start size:84% position:16%
and he didn't
really seem to know

00:17:36.055 --> 00:17:37.423
what the hell he was signing.

00:17:37.423 --> 00:17:39.124 align:start size:97% position:3%
- No, he didn't.
- And when you think of them,

00:17:39.124 --> 00:17:41.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
they were all sitting
there waiting to be signed

00:17:41.393 --> 00:17:43.362
and they were radical.

00:17:43.362 --> 00:17:44.730
They were radical.

00:17:44.730 --> 00:17:46.899
They were Bernie Sanders
would have never asked

00:17:46.899 --> 00:17:49.068 align:start size:84% position:16%
for most of the things
that he is signing.

00:17:49.068 --> 00:17:53.305 align:start size:97% position:3%
